/* == Homepage TravelTools section width (tpa-*) 2026-08-21 ==
   Quote desk sat inside extra left/right gap vs SellerTools / HowItWorks /
   Toolkit / JourneyNumbers. Cause: laptop .tpa-fit-zoom (1024–1919) is a
   real flex box with zoom: 0.85 and width: 100% — CSS zoom shrinks used
   width to 85% of the section, so container-page no longer matches siblings.
   Do not inflate by 1/0.85 (that overflow-clipped the right minis).
   Keep width: 100%. Wrapper is display:contents so .container-page is the
   same gutter as other landing sections: section-curve-sticky
   margin-inline clamp(0.25rem, 0.65vw, 0.5rem) + container-page
   max-width 94rem + padding-inline clamp(0.875rem, 1.5vw, 1.75rem).
   No extra mx / padding-inline on .tpa-section / .tpa-fit-zoom / .tpa-shell.
   Column-ratio + title wrap in this band unchanged. No wheel trap, no 340vh.
   SellerTools / .sto-* untouched. */

.tpa-section {
  padding-inline: 0;
}

.tpa-fit-zoom {
  margin-inline: 0;
  padding-inline: 0;
}

@media (min-width: 1024px) and (max-width: 1919px) {
  .tpa-fit-zoom {
    display: contents;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 100%;
    margin-inline: 0;
    padding-inline: 0;
    zoom: unset;
  }

  .tpa-fit-zoom > .tpa-shell {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: min(100%, 94rem);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
}

